    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="1039" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.67/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-13T17:00:00+02:00">February 13, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Department’s No. 18, February 9, 3 p.m. Extradition Treaty presented National
                    Assembly November 25 and will be ratified during next session beginning March
                        1st.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d787-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d787-f1" n="53" xml:id="d787-f1-content">
                <p>Ratified by the President of the United States, February 21, 1934; ratified by
                    Turkey, May 8, 1934; ratifications exchanged at Ankara, June 18, 1934;
                    proclaimed by the President of the United States, August 18, 1934. Department of
                    State Treaty Series No. 872.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
